BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Patterns of Belonging: Creating Repeating Patterns
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T153000
UID:6ac7d647e8cf1c005cb0dc33@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​This   hands-on workshop introduces participants to the sim
 ple principles behind   repeat pattern design and invites them to create a
  pattern inspired by   something meaningful to them. Using a small hand-de
 signed motif as a starting   point\, participants will learn how a single 
 image can be transformed into a   repeating pattern through rotation\, ref
 lection\, repetition and arrangement.\nAge Group: YA\, ADULT 18-24\, 25-6
 4\, 65+
LOCATION:Scarborough Civic Centre\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7d647e8cf1c005cb0dc33
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists Circle: Geometric Art and Watercolours
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T153000
UID:6ab14078f5c6780c704967d6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an e
 xtensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heav
 ily on tools such as a protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this works
 hop\, participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-st
 ep instructions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their 
 own geometric pattern and complex design art pieces. All materials will be
  provided and no experience is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nGeometric watercolour ar
 t example.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab14078f5c6780c704967d6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
