BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sultan and the Detective: Sherlock Holmes’ Curious Adventure
 s in the Ottoman Empire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T160000
UID:6a91cd3f57c264087ad483e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Friends of the Arthur Conan Doyle Collection: 2026 Cameron
  Hollyer Memorial Lecture\nHistorical fact: the last great Ottoman sultan\
 , Abdülhamid II\, fell asleep each night to the adventures of Sherlock Ho
 lmes\, read aloud to him by a palace attendant. This unlikely obsession is
  the starting point for Andrew Finkel's novel\nThe Adventure of the Second
  Wife.\nIn this talk\, Finkel explores how the world of Arthur Conan Doyle
  intersected with the late Ottoman Empire\, and what this reveals about st
 orytelling\, translation\, and the unexpected ways stories travel across l
 anguages\, cultures\, and empires to take on meanings the author never int
 ended.\nAndrew Finkel is a journalist and author who has reported from Tur
 key for major international outlets including\nThe Times\, The Economist\,
  TIME\, CNN\,\nand\nThe New York Times\n. He co-founded Platform24 (P24)\,
  an Istanbul-based NGO that supports independent journalism and freedom of
  expression\, and is the author of\nTurkey: What Everyone Needs to Know\n.
 \nAdmission is Free. All are welcome. Please note\, refreshments will be 
 provided at this event.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91cd3f57c264087ad483e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
