SUMMARY:Islamic Geometric Art & Watercolors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T150000
UID:6ac7a6649d27a000454f7e16@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as a protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this worksho
 p\, participants will be guided through step-by-step instructions using dr
 awing tools and watercolour paint to create their own geometric pattern an
 d complex design art pieces.
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park\, Program room (main floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7a6649d27a000454f7e16
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
