DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6ab6ce03101eb7003f32ebfe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThis workshop maps out the funding pathwa
 ys available to Black entrepreneurs\, including grants\, microloans\, and 
 community lenders. Participants learn what funders look for\, which comes 
 down to readiness\, a clear story\, and credible numbers. A live walkthrou
 gh then demonstrates how to prepare a simple funding application of their 
 own.\nDrop-In\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident ent
 repreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/ei
 r\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until availab
 le slots are filled.
