BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marlon James: The Disappearers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T200000
UID:6a85b7bd2f41840bbfc30784@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents Booker Prize-winning author Marlon James in conve
 rsation with Kamal Al-Solaylee at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Sa
 lon.\nIn his triumphant return to the Jamaica of his Booker Prize-winning\
 nA Brief History of Seven Killings\n\, Marlon James delivers\nThe Disappea
 rers\n\, an epic\, unflinching novel about survival in the aftermath of vi
 olence. Written with the language-rich\, urgent style that has made James 
 one of the most acclaimed novelists working today\, this is a story of men
  forced to make impossible compromises to survive a society that demands t
 heir erasure.\nAt once a detective story and a searing sociocultural histo
 ry\,\nThe Disappearers\nplunges into the tragic\, ongoing consequences of 
 violent homophobia\, rendering its characters' inner lives with the vivid 
 imagery\, sharp dialogue\, and unrelenting energy that have defined James'
 s celebrated body of work.\nJoin one of the most acclaimed novelists of hi
 s generation\, in conversation with Kamal Al-Solaylee\, for an evening exp
 loring rage\, resilience\, and the price of queer solidarity in a world bu
 ilt to deny it.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purch
 ase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nMarlon James\nKamal Al-Solaylee\nRead 
 more:\nThe Disappearers\nA Brief History of Seven Killings\nReturn\n***\nP
 LAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference
  Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event 
 starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe 
 oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an
  opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity 
 is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available
  for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to ac
 cessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to reques
 t accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca 
 or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event 
 is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and interna
 tional authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about their new book
 s and big ideas.\nThis event is also part of TPL's\nBlack History and Cult
 ure\nSeries.\nPresenting Sponsor of Heritage Programs: TD Bank Group\, thr
 ough the TD Ready Commitment.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey 
 following the program. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b7bd2f41840bbfc30784
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
