BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newcomer Welcome Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T153000
UID:6ab6c2928cf597003f9665c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Kensington-Chinatown Local Immigration Partnership present
 s our annual Newcomer Welcome Fair! Join us for a film screening\, informa
 tive talks on topics relevant to newcomers\, performances\, and more. Whil
 e you're here\, visit the community tables to learn about local newcomer-s
 erving organizations.\nEvents include:\n- Lion dance (Chinatown Community 
 Lion Dance)\n- Film screening of Butter Chicken to Go and Restaurant Kids 
 (National Film Board)\n- Talk: Impacts of recent immigration law changes (
 South Asian Legal Clinic of Ontario)\n- Talk: Impacts of public health car
 e changes (Ontario Health Coalition)\n- Talk: Economic benefits of public 
 healthcare (Centre for Future Work)\n- Performance: Singer-songwriter Gina
 lina\n- Talk: AI use and immigrants in workplaces (Dr. Guang Ying Mo)\n- I
 nfo session: Hepatitis C & B (CATIE)\n- Workshop: Zine making (Toronto Pub
 lic Library)\n- Performance: Inner Truth Taiko Dojo\nRefreshments provided
  and prizes offered. Drop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6c2928cf597003f9665c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: In Person Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T160000
UID:6aa4700c4b3b060030831dca@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oin\na Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event 
 series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid em
 ail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles.
 \nAttend all four sessions in person at\nNorthern District Library\n.\nReg
 istration is a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complete thei
 r registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will fol
 low up to request additional information in order to complete the registra
 tion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa4700c4b3b060030831dca
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
