DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T160000
UID:6a0622accaf93436005beec6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nFri
 day\, October 16\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a week fo
 r 8 weeks\, October 23 to December 11\n. Registration closes after week 3\
 , or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshm
 ents are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availabl
 e at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis 
 Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible f
 or the protection of \npersonal information collected through the program 
 registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Room B1\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0622accaf93436005beec6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
