BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Daniel Schlick
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T235959
UID:6aac651da433d308573bf1c2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of October\, the works of artist Daniel S
 chlick are on display at Northern District library.\nDaniel Schlick is a m
 ultidisciplinary artist and photographer based in Toronto\, Canada. Curren
 tly studying at OCAD University\, his practice draws inspiration from trav
 el\, philosophy\, and everyday experiences. Through photography and other 
 media\, Schlick explores the relationship between art\, life\, perception\
 , and observation\, guided by the idea that art reflects life while existi
 ng for its own purpose.\n"My photographic project follows confrontations w
 ith silence and searches for ruptures in the everyday world through which 
 can be witnessed an unsettling sublimity. The monumentality of my works is
  equalled by the gravity of their presence\, both tranquil and uncanny. I 
 believe that photography's\npotency is its ability to investigate our inti
 macy with the world that surrounds us and to discover in it a very persona
 l truth\, the truth of what we desire\nfrom that very intimacy."\nThis exh
 ibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library 
 provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across
  the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of
  the city and its neighborhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Norther
 n District library's open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nCredit: by Dani
 el Schlick
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor Art Gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac651da433d308573bf1c2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
