BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: "Pools of Presence: Meditative Collages and Ph
 otographs" by Catherine Raine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T235959
UID:6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Catherine Raine
  are on display at Don Mills Branch in an exhibit titled "Pools of Presen
 ce: Meditative Collages and Photographs."\nCatherine Raine loves collage-m
 aking\, nature photography\, and writing poetry. Motivated to share these 
 loves with others\, Catherine has exhibited her artwork in Toronto and Ka
 nsas City as well as published poems in 'Writers Unblocked' Vol. 1 (2 & 3)
  and 'Mindful Poetry Moments' (6th ed). Connecting artistic practice with
  mental wellness\, Catherine has self-published 'Visualizations for Heartb
 reak: Words\, Photographs\, and Collage.'\n"'Pools of Presence: Meditative
  Collages and Photographs" captures moments of deep attention like watchin
 g raindrops dive into a puddle or creating a\nshoreline from buttons. This
  exhibit also celebrates mindfulness by inviting viewers to contemplate ri
 verside grasses\, a woman with a bundle\, a pensive\nswan\, and many other
  images.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toro
 nto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work 
 at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cu
 ltural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be v
 iewed during Don Mills branch open hours. Please check the\nDon Mills\nb
 ranch page before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Racheal McCaig
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T235959
UID:6abef55ac6cddb0045955ec1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of October\, the works of artist Racheal 
 McCaig are on display at Albion Branch.\nRacheal is an arts insider and 
 award-winning photojournalist\, Racheal’s work takes her behind the scen
 es and around the world. While she loves creating dynamic moments\, she t
 ruly delights in capturing the beauty in the every day. Along with being t
 he recipient of two medals of honour from the Government of France\, she 
 is also an active advocate for the arts.\n"We wear them every November\, b
 ut how many of us have actually seen a poppy? As the audience explores the
  impact and history of these delicate\, fragile flowers\, the installatio
 n will also create a sense of calm as they move through it. Tiens-le haut 
 is a new creation proving that something fragile can stand for strength."\
 nThe exhibit can be viewed during Albion branch's open hours. Please check
  the\nAlbion branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto
  credit: Racheal McCaig\,\nRM Tiens-le haut Poppy Series 163A8195\, Extra
  Large.
LOCATION:Albion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abef55ac6cddb0045955ec1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ukulele Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T153000
UID:6ada273dfee2d21deb25051f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun while learning to play a new instrument: the ukule
 le! In this beginner-friendly ukulele series\, learn all the basics of pl
 aying ukulele\, including the instrument's parts\, tuning\, simple strumm
 ing patterns\, and easy chords. Enjoy fun music games\, group singing and
  beginner songwriting activities while playing music together. No experie
 nce needed and a limited supply of ukuleles will be provided.
