DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service\nThrough a lecture and open Q&A supported b
 y practical checklists\, this workshop explains how to register a business
  in Ontario and helps participants choose between operating as a sole pro
 prietor and incorporating. It covers licenses and permits\, CRA basics suc
 h as HST and the business number\, and insurance. It closes with the regul
 atory pitfalls new owners most often fall into and how to avoid them.\nDro
 p-In\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur
 \, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We b
 egin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots 
 are filled.
