BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creating a Landing Page: Tell Your Story and Track Your Customers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6a99bb084995480655ed74ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nYou don't need a full website when y
 ou're getting started with a new business\, one page can get the job done.
  This session covers what a landing page should contain\, how to attract c
 ustomers\, and how to inform them about your product. During the session\,
  we will look at free tools that don't require coding knowledge\, learn ho
 w to collect emails\, and learn how to assess if a business page is functi
 oning correctly.\nThe program includes a short networking component\, prov
 iding participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs
 .\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reach
 ed.\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\
 , Ryan\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We b
 egin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots 
 are filled.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb084995480655ed74ce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T203000
UID:6ac7b588686221156abba69b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\,\nThursdays Nov. 5\, 12\, 19 and 26 from 6-8:30pm.\nRegi
 stration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete their r
 egistration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow
  up to request additional information in order to complete the registratio
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7b588686221156abba69b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
