BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library:  Cardinal Flower Felt Collage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T200000
UID:6a7f610360ccaf01c01e449d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 3 of a series of workshops for adults\, exploring local f
 lora through embroidery and felt collage.  This event is part of the\nAr
 tists in the Library\nprogram\, hosted by Artist\, Sarah Zanchetta.\nRegis
 tration is required. Space is limited.\nPlease note: Registered participan
 t spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which drop-ins will be allowed.
 \nMeet the Resident:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) is a queer textile artist
  and educator whose practice dives into the loss of connection and knowled
 ge of poisonous plants in North America. Zanchetta uses textiles\, texts\,
  and hosts community workshops to create intimate works and spaces where w
 e can unfold our curiosities\, care and anxieties about what grows beside 
 our feet. She holds a Master of Visual Studies from the University of Tor
 onto (2023) and a BFA from OCAD University (2018).\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f610360ccaf01c01e449d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
