BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culture and Technology Book Club : Killed by a Traffic Engineer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T200000
UID:6a95d29d3b6c71003e5caee5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Culture and Technology Book club brings readers together e
 very two months to discuss new and classic texts that raise important ques
 tions about the way technology transforms our cultural and political lives
 .\nThis meeting we'll discuss:\nKilled by A Traffic Engineer\n(also availa
 ble as an audiobook)\nCivil Engineering professor Wes Marshal takes a hard
  look at how traffic engineering standards in North America have shaped o
 ur streets for the worse. He examines some of the dubious and unscientific
  assumptions central to traffic engineering such as their fixation on spe
 ed. Marshal asks what it might look like to build transportation infrastr
 ucture with a more holistic understanding of people's needs.\nRegister for
  this program to receive the discussion questions a week in advance of the
  meeting.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, in the elearning lab (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95d29d3b6c71003e5caee5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
