BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hank Idsinga: The High Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T200000
UID:6a85b934f564ef0d72c0eb91@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents retired homicide detective and author Hank Idsing
 a in conversation with Wendy Gillis at the North York Central Library's Co
 ncourse Event Space.\nIn his bestselling memoir\nThe High Road: Confession
 s of a Homicide Cop\n\, Idsinga takes readers behind the crime scene tape 
 and into the mean streets of Toronto's most notorious murders. Teaming up 
 with partners including future police chief Mark Saunders\, Idsinga built 
 a reputation for excellent recall and sharp instinct\, finding motive and 
 method faster than most. As the public face of that investigation\, Idsing
 a remained strong and compassionate before the cameras\, even as the polic
 e force faced fierce criticism over its handling of the case.\nHow do homi
 cide detectives carry the weight of the cases they never solve? What does 
 real accountability within policing actually look like\, and why does it m
 atter? And what can three decades on the front lines of Toronto's worst cr
 imes teach us about justice\, institutional trust\, and the human cost of 
 violence?\nJoin veteran crime reporter Wendy Gillis in conversation with H
 ank Idsinga for a gripping\, candid evening inside the world of Canada's m
 ost storied homicide unit.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books availabl
 e for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nHank Idsinga\nWendy Gillis\
 nRead more:\nThe High Road\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nConcourse Ev
 ent Space\, North York Central Library (5120 Yonge St)\, Lower Level\nTime
 :\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration r
 equired.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the grea
 test number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed un
 til 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served
 .\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you are Deaf or h
 ave a disability and would like to request accommodation for this event\, 
 please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three we
 eks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nOn Civi
 l Society\nseries\, where we host local and international authors\, activi
 sts and academics in conversation about the most critical topics of our ti
 me. Generously supported by the McConnell Foundation and also by Chris M. 
 Reid.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Regist
 rants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space\, North York C
 entral Library (5120 Yonge St)\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b934f564ef0d72c0eb91
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
