BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Diabetes Myths and Facts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T130000
UID:6ac6a3499d27a000454f55a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Living with diabetes or prediabetes can come with a lot of inf
 ormation about what to eat\, what to avoid\, and how to manage your blood 
 sugar. With so much advice out there\, it can be difficult to separate fac
 t from fiction or know where to focus.\nJoin Catherine Cai\, Registered Di
 etitian and Certified Diabetes Educator\, for a practical and interactive 
 session that separates fact from fiction and explores realistic ways to be
 tter understand and manage diabetes and prediabetes.\nWhat to Expect\nUnde
 rstanding Blood Sugar:\nLearn what your levels mean and how an A1C test pr
 ovides a picture of your average levels over time.\nDiabetes Myths and Fac
 ts:\nExplore common myths      and misconceptions about diabetes and separ
 ate fact from fiction.\nLifestyle and Blood Sugar:\nLearn how sleep\,     
  stress and other lifestyle factors can affect blood sugar.\nBuilding Bala
 nced Meals:\nLearn practical ways      to build balanced\, diabetes-friend
 ly meals.\nBalance\, Not Perfection:\nExplore how balance      and consist
 ency can support diabetes management without striving for      perfection.
 \nAbout the Presenter\nCatherine Cai is a Registered Dietitian and Certifi
 ed Diabetes Educator at Crosstown Family Health Team. She provides practic
 al information and guidance to help people better understand nutrition and
  support their health.\nThis program is presented by Toronto Public Librar
 y in collaboration with the West Toronto Ontario Health Team (OHT)\, a net
 work of over 40 local health and social service providers working together
  to improve the health and well-being of communities in West Toronto.\nYou
 r Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour
  Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted health programs and res
 ources to help people make informed decisions about their health. Learn mo
 re by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nReserve Your Spot To
 day!\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join but registration is required
 . Once registered\, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nWe can
 ’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac6a3499d27a000454f55a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
