SUMMARY:Tools to Run Your Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T200000
UID:6a99bb28660e510bf4410247@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nFor new business owners\, staying or
 ganized can be just as challenging to find customers. This session will ex
 plore the tools that can take routine work off your plate. From bookkeepin
 g and invoicing\, to scheduling\, payments\, customer records\, marketing\
 , and social media creation. We will also look at where AI tools can genui
 nely help save time and add value versus making unnecessary work. We'll di
 scover where to find free resources\, and how to avoid subscribing to serv
 ices that won't be of value in the long run. You'll leave with a concise l
 ist of tools appropriate for new business owners.\nThe program includes a 
 short networking component\, providing participants with an opportunity to
  connect with other entrepreneurs.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins wel
 come until room capacity is reached.\nTo apply for one-on-one consultation
 s with our resident entrepreneur\, Ryan\, please fill out the in-take form
  available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September
  28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb28660e510bf4410247
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
