DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residenc\ne (EIR) service\nIn this interactive workshop\, participan
 ts define their brand story and state their value in plain language\, shar
 pening it through a message-crafting exercise. The session focuses on mark
 eting that costs little but works well\, such as word of mouth\, community
  partnerships\, and local events. It also shows how to turn first customer
 s into repeat customers and a steady source of referrals.\nDrop-In\nTo app
 ly for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Leo\, ple
 ase fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepti
 ng in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.
