 orkshop will build on the crochet techniques learned in the      last work
 shop\, tackling the half double crochet\, double crochet\, and the      tr
 eble crochet stitches.\nNovember      18:\nThis workshop is a self-led cro
 chet session to make space for      participants to create their patches f
 or the communal tapestry. Workshop      materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants.\nNovember      25:\nThis workshop is a self-led cr
 ochet session to make space for      participants to finish their patches 
 for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches t
 o the communal tapestry as they are      completed.\nRegistration required
 . W\norkshop materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Fee
 l free to drop-in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll al
 so reflect on and discuss our connections to crochet\, air\, and our commu
 nities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
