BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food Justice in Toronto: Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6ac3e146a85a2c00337d59a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join an expert-led discussion on food justice in your communit
 y. Learn about Toronto's food system\, the issues that affect our food acc
 ess\, and strategies to address food insecurity and inequity. The panel wi
 ll be followed by a facilitated group discussion reflecting on engagement 
 with local food systems and practices.\nPanelists include:\nShath Ramesh\n
 (she/they) is a community organizer and the Urban Agriculture Coordinator 
 at Malvern Family Resource Centre\, where they manage the Malvern Urban Fa
 rmers' Market. They hold a Masters in sustainability studies from Trent Un
 iversity and are passionate about food justice\, climate action and advoca
 cy.\nJade Guthrie\n(she/her) is a queer\, mixed-race educator\, facilitat
 or\, and community organizer. As the Manager of Community Learning and Eng
 agement at FoodShare Toronto\, jade is committed to social change work roo
 ted in justice\, liberation\, and joy and approaches this work with tender
 ness\, curiosity\, and reciprocity. Beyond 9-5\, jade is an organizer with
  Justicia for Migrant Workers\, a board member at Food Secure Canada\, and
  sits on the City of Toronto’s Black Food Sovereignty Action Plan Adviso
 ry Circle.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac3e146a85a2c00337d59a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
