BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture théâtre avec le Théâtre français de Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6ad13d42377296003a4c46b7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:La Bibliothèque publique de Toronto et le\nThéâtre françai
 s de Toronto\ns'associent pour créer un club de lecture théâtre. Ce ren
 dez-vous mensuel est l'occasion de discuter et d'explorer des scènes myth
 iques ayant marqué le monde du théâtre. Avec\nGeorges Som\n\, médiateu
 r culturel\, nous essayerons de comprendre les enjeux de ces scènes\, de 
 découvrir leurs sens et de partager nos sentiments sur leurs auteurs et a
 utrices. Chacun est le bienvenu au club\, qu'il soit néophyte ou amateur 
 de théâtre confirmé. Les seuls prérequis pour participer sont la curio
 sité et le plaisir d'échanger autour du théâtre !\nAu mois de novembre
 \, nous allons discuter un extrait de la pièce\nPapa doit manger\nde Mari
 e Ndiyae.  Papa est parti depuis si longtemps que personne n'espère plu
 s son retour. Mais voilà que Papa revient\, voilà que Papa exige de rent
 rer\, sûr de son bon droit\, dans la vie qu'il a fuie dix ans auparavant.
  Qui aime encore Papa? Qui peut prétendre avoir besoin de lui? Il a les a
 pparences de la richesse et d'une jeunesse improbable. Il resplendit d'un 
 éclat peu commun à Courbevoie. Surtout\, il sait ce qu'on lui doit\, mê
 me si ce n'est pas justifié\, et qu'on l'aime encore\, qu'on l'aimera tou
 jours.\nInformation Collection Notice\n:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.\nACCESSIBILITÉ\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, 
 l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’intervenant\, 
 ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez 
 soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à :\ntpl.ca/
 accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3e étage
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad13d42377296003a4c46b7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6a6a661db57350d760b31f44@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet online every Thursday evening\,\nSeptember 24 - De
 cember 10\, 6-7:30 PM\n(12 sessions).\nParticipants are expected to commit
  to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekly basis.\nLea
 rners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digital badge\ndown
 load a certificate of completion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f44
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Imagining a Turtle Named Franklin by Brenda Clark
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T193000
UID:6a7f61303f18f80030bb245a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Photo credit: Lee Higginson.\nJoin the Osborne Collection of E
 arly Children's Books for our 19th Annual Sybille Pantazzi Memorial Lectur
 e: Imagining a Turtle Named Franklin by Brenda Clark.\nAward winning pictu
 re book illustrator\, Brenda Clark is the original illustrator of the belo
 ved Franklin the Turtle book series\, by author Paulette Bourgeois. In thi
 s lecture\, she will share how she became an artist and how Franklin was c
 reated. Brenda’s illustrations have played a key role in Franklin’s wo
 rldwide popularity\, leading to the inspiration of the animated TV series\
 , merchandise\, spin-off books\, a children’s garden on Toronto Island a
 nd a Canadian postage stamp. She will walk us through the process of desig
 ning and painting the art and explain how it takes some amazing teamwork t
 o meet the challenges of Franklin’s success.\nFor the past 40 years\, Br
 enda Clark has delighted children as the illustrator of the hugely success
 ful Franklin the Turtle children’s book series. Over 70 million Franklin
  books have been sold in more than 30 languages worldwide\, making it the 
 single most successful picture book series in the history of Canadian publ
 ishing. In 2011\, the archives of Brenda Clark were donated to the Osborne
  Collection of Early Children’s Books\, and recognized by the Canadian C
 ultural Property Export Review Board as cultural property for its “Outst
 anding Significance and National Importance”. In 2014\, Brenda was named
  a Member of the Order of Canada. She lives in Port Hope\, Ontario.\nBook 
 signings will take place before the lecture from 5:00-6:00 pm on the 4th f
 loor in the Osborne Collection.\nFranklin in the Dark
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Lower Level- Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f61303f18f80030bb245a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
