BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hazel Mae: Before I Let You Go
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T200000
UID:6a85b6abf564ef0d72c0eb1f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Host Update:\nLegendary Canadian broadcaster Melissa Grelo is 
 now hosting this event. Due to unforeseen circumstances\, Ernie Clement is
  no longer able to participate.\nBeloved Toronto Blue Jays sportscaster Ha
 zel Mae shares her open and insightful new memoir.\nIn Before I Let You Go
 \, Mae invites us into a candid\, behind-the-scenes look at her life\, fro
 m her early days in the Philippines to her arrival in Canada and her rise 
 through the ranks of sports journalism.\nWith warmth and wit\, she reflect
 s on breaking into broadcasting\, navigating the US sports media scene\, r
 eturning home to cover the Toronto Blue Jays\, and mastering the art of th
 e post game interview—often while dodging celebratory Gatorade showers.\
 nHazel Mae speaks with broadcaster Melissa Grelo about her memoir and life
  as one of Canada's most recognizable broadcasters.\nQ&A and book signing 
 to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nHa
 zel Mae\nMelissa Grelo\nRead more:\nBefore I Let You Go : My Life in Broad
 casting\, Baseball\, and Beyond\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram an
 d Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd f
 loor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree regi
 stration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure tha
 t the greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets gua
 ranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, fi
 rst served.\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\n
 ***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host l
 ocal and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation abou
 t their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief surv
 ey following the program. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b6abf564ef0d72c0eb1f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) - Hope + Me
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T200000
UID:6ab418b16074830038290959@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Come to a\nvirtual information session\non\
 nOctober 8th at 5-6pm\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\,\nonce a wee
 k for 8 weeks\, October 15 to December 3\n. Registration closes after week
  3\, or when full. Note\, in order to obtain a WRAP certificate at the en
 d of the 8 weeks\, participants need to attend all eight sessions.\nTTC Pr
 esto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for a
 ll participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis
  program is in collaboration with Hope + Me. Hope + Me is solely respons
 ible for the protection of personal information collected through the prog
 ram registration process.\nPlease visit the\nHope and Me website to regist
 er
LOCATION:Richview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab418b16074830038290959
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T203000
UID:6ac7b588686221156abba69c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\,\nThursdays Nov. 5\, 12\, 19 and 26 from 6-8:30pm.\nRegi
 stration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete their r
 egistration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follow
  up to request additional information in order to complete the registratio
 n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7b588686221156abba69c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
