BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ghost Stories of Toronto: Séances & The World Wars
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T130000
UID:6a85b74d4c610f0038954f48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Séances were all the rage a century ago. Having begun to fall
  out of fashion in the early 1900s\, they experienced a resurgence after t
 he deadly years of the First World War and the Spanish Flu as people held 
 out hope they could still communicate with their lost loved ones. In the t
 hird lecture of this series by author Adam Bunch\, we'll explore the histo
 ry of séances during those turbulent times\, from those who truly believe
 d in their power\, to the fraudsters who preyed on a grieving city\, to th
 e prime minister who took advice from the spirits of the dead.\nAbout this
  event's guest:\nAdam Bunch\nRead More:\nThe Toronto Book of Love\nThe Tor
 onto Book of the Dead\nAbout this series:\nYou can learn a lot about Toron
 to through its ghost stories. Whether you believe in the supernatural or n
 ot\, the tales we tell about spirits and spectres illuminate the true hist
 ory of the city. They're often tied to dramatic stories of death and disas
 ter\, to fascinating historic sites\, and to pivotal moments that helped s
 hape our communities. In this series of talks by author Adam Bunch\, we'll
  explore Toronto's past through tales of ghosts\, séances and hauntings. 
 Whether it's phantom horses from the War of 1812\, the strange prime minis
 ter who believed in the occult\, or the ghost who was arrested by the Toro
 nto Police Morality Squad\, these supernatural stories have a lot to teach
  us about the history of the place we call home.\n***\nImportant informati
 on for accessing this live virtual event:\nYou must register for a free ti
 cket via Eventbrite to gain access to this event.\nThis event will be pres
 ented in a Zoom Webinar. Once registered\, you will receive reminder email
 s from both Zoom and Eventbrite with links and instructions to access your
  unique Zoom Webinar link to watch this event.\nAt the time of the event\,
  you must be signed in to Zoom or Eventbrite with the same email address t
 hat you used to book your ticket in order to access your unique event link
 . Unique event links can only be open on one device at a time.\n***\nAcces
 sibility at Toronto Public Library\nWe are committed to making our content
  accessible to as many Torontonians as possible. Please call or email us i
 f you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommodatio
 n to participate in this program. Please let us know as far in advance as 
 possible and we will do our best to meet your request. At least three week
 s' notice is preferred. Phone 416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl
 .ca\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistr
 ants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program\n. 
 Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed t
 o Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b74d4c610f0038954f48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
