BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rachel Cusk: Life of M
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
UID:6a85b6d72cbfe80d71a4733b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Critically acclaimed author Rachel Cusk shares her irresistibl
 e new novel.\nLife of M introduces us to movie star M\, one of the most re
 cognizable faces of our time\, whose image has been ubiquitous since she w
 as a child.\nWith such fame\, her life has the appearance of freedom: peop
 le are instantly obliging\, spaces are altered to accommodate her\, time c
 an be rearranged. M may live in the same places as real people. She may me
 et her friends or collect her children from school or walk her dogs as the
 y do. But it seems the rules of reality have melted away.\nNow\, a writer 
 has decided to pay close attention to M’s life in the hope of understand
 ing who she really is. It is hard not to feel ugly next to M\, hard not to
  feel insignificant. But what truths―about the very experience of living
 ―might this proximity allow the writer to briefly capture?\nRachel Cusk 
 speaks with Sheila Heti about Life of M\, an astonishing new novel about f
 ame\, power\, beauty\, and truth\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books av
 ailable for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nRachel Cusk\nSheila H
 eti\nRead more:\nLife of M : A Novel\nOutline\nAlphabetical Diaries\nPure 
 Colour\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Tor
 onto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6
 :00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicke
 t policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of 
 people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or u
 ntil capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar:\nBeer/w
 ine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\n***\nThis event is part o
 f our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and international au
 thors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about their new books and big
  ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Regi
 strants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
 to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b6d72cbfe80d71a4733b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Selling with Confidence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T200000
UID:6ab6d13e65abe8002a7c13ee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nThis practice-based workshop covers the f
 undamentals of selling: listening well\, communicating value\, and followi
 ng up. Participants learn to handle pricing conversations and respond to t
 he common "it's too expensive" objection. Through roleplay\, each particip
 ant practices a 60-second pitch of their business live\, with coaching on 
 the spot.\nDrop-In\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our residen
 t entrepreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.
 ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until av
 ailable slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d13e65abe8002a7c13ee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
