BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ageing In Place: How To Assess Your Long Term Care Options
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
UID:6ab1ba6b129d8e0031f41d0f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Where do you want to spend your retirement years and how can y
 ou make that happen?\nLooking ahead and having a plan gives us control. Ra
 ther than leaving things up to chance\, we get to make the choices and dec
 isions that we want--not that someone else wants. Karen Henderson\, an ex
 pert in long term care options\, shares her knowledge and resources to hel
 p you make more informed decisions.\nAs the result of a life changing 14-y
 ear dementia care experience\, Karen founded the Long Term Care Planning N
 etwork\, Canada’s leading resource centre for ageing\, eldercare and lon
 g term care planning and education. Her seminar series\, web site and prin
 t/electronic tools are recognized as key long term care educational resour
 ces for Canadian families.\nKaren is a Certified Professional Consultant o
 n Aging (CPCA).
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab1ba6b129d8e0031f41d0f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
