 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 3\, 2-4 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Saturday morni
 ng\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 10 - November 28\, 2:00-4:45 pm\nR
 egistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will b
 e provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. In
 gredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisi
 s Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal informatio
 n collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4e8a137d04302f001671ba
