BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bee-ing a Pollinator Protector: Plan Now for a Buzzing Spring Gard
 en
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T200000
UID:6abc355e035faf0033d93386@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Saving the bees is an environmental cause that resonates deepl
 y with Canadians.  While most of us might not be thinking about bees this 
 time of year\, our actions during the colder months can still support thes
 e pollinators\, particularly native bees\, which are crucial and threatene
 d by climate change\, habitat loss\, and other pressures.\nIn honour of th
 e late bee scientist Sheila Colla\, this presentation will offer practical
  tips on planting and maintaining gardens that provide beautifully bloomin
 g habitat for pollinators\, with a particular focus on how native plants s
 upport wild bees.\nPresented by\nLorraine Johnson\n\, who co-authored\nA G
 arden for the Rusty-Patched Bumblebee\nwith Sheila Colla\, as part of TPL'
 s environmental program series\,\nOur Fragile Planet\n\, supported by Frie
 nds of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nFree. Register for a re
 minder.\nDoors open at 6:30 pm for attendees to mingle\, chat with Lorrain
 e\, and explore related resources. Presentation begins at 7:00 pm.\nPlace 
 a hold or borrow from Toronto Public Library:\nA Garden for the Rusty-patc
 hed Bumblebee\n(book)\nA Garden for the Rusty-Patched Bumblebee\n(ebook)\n
 This program will also be offered virtually on\nTuesday\, November 3\, 202
 6\n\, from 7:00 pm to 8:00 pm\, as part of Climate Action Week. To registe
 r for the online program and for more info\, see the\nlisting\n.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc355e035faf0033d93386
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
