BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Breast Cancer Screening and Early Detection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
UID:6ad250ff035faf0033dd15e3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Breast cancer is one of the most common cancers affecting wome
 n\, but early detection can significantly improve outcomes. Understanding 
 your risk\, knowing when to get screened\, and recognizing potential warni
 ng signs are important steps in protecting your health.\nWhat to Expect:\n
 Understanding Breast Cancer:\nLearn about breast cancer\, who may be at ri
 sk\, and ways to help reduce your risk.\nScreening and Early Detection:\nU
 nderstand who should be screened\, why early detection matters\, and what 
 to expect during the screening process.\nRecognizing Warning Signs:\nLearn
  about potential signs and symptoms of breast cancer and the role of breas
 t self-examination and assessment.\nAccessing Care and Support:\nLearn abo
 ut the Ontario Breast Screening Program and resources available to support
  people living with breast cancer.\nThis session will be led by staff from
  LAMP Community Health Centre\, who will provide practical information and
  guidance to help you better understand breast cancer screening and the re
 sources available to support your health.\nThis program is presented by To
 ronto Public Library in collaboration with the West Toronto Ontario Health
  Team (OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service provide
 rs working together to improve the health and well-being of communities in
  West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Publi
 c Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted heal
 th programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about the
 ir health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nR
 eserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join but regis
 tration is required. Once registered\, you’ll receive an email with the 
 Zoom link.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad250ff035faf0033dd15e3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
