BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeff Chang: Bruce Lee and the Making of Asian America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6a85b7fa1401fd00606cea3c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents award-winning author Jeff Chang in conversation w
 ith Vinh Nguyen at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Salon\, celebrati
 ng what would have been Bruce Lee's birthday.\nMore than half a century af
 ter his death\, Bruce Lee remains as towering a figure as ever\, the man w
 ho popularized martial arts in the West\, became a bridge between Eastern 
 and Western culture\, and was poised to conquer Hollywood when he died sud
 denly at age thirty-two. But in the decades since\, his legend has eclipse
 d the man. Forgotten is the immigrant\, the fighter\, the seeker\, the tea
 cher\, the father grappling with exile and belonging in a country that que
 stioned his right to simply exist.\nIn his epic new cultural biography\nWa
 ter Mirror Echo: Bruce Lee and the Making of Asian America\n\, acclaimed a
 uthor Jeff Chang recovers the man behind the icon. Drawing on in-depth int
 erviews with Lee's closest intimates\, thousands of newly available person
 al documents\, and dozens of rare photographs from the family archive\, Ch
 ang traces Lee's remarkable journey: a charismatic child star turned delin
 quent teen fighter in Hong Kong\, exiled alone to America\, who transforme
 d personal struggle into a philosophy of movement and being. Chang reveals
  how Lee's rise didn't just create a Hollywood legend\, it helped birth so
 mething even more enduring: the very concept of Asian America.\nJoin Jeff 
 Chang for a special evening honouring Bruce Lee's birthday\, offering a st
 irringly human portrait of the icon\, the immigrant\, and the movement he 
 unknowingly ignited.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for 
 purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nJeff Chang\nVinh Nguyen\nRead mor
 e:\nWater Mirror Echo\nCan't Stop Won't Stop\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocat
 ion:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge St
 reet)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTicket
 s:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events 
 to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend
 . Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating fi
 rst come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for purchase (debit/c
 redit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you ar
 e Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommodation for th
 is event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at lea
 st three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signatu
 re\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and international authors\, artis
 ts and thinkers in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\nThis
  event is also part of TPL's\nAsian Heritage\nSeries.\nPresenting Sponsor 
 of Heritage Programs: TD Bank Group\, through the TD Ready Commitment.\n**
 *\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may
  be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b7fa1401fd00606cea3c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
