BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get Ready to Launch Your Business: Keep Up the Momentum and Find t
 he Money
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6a99bba4341bb11431eea279@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nWe're wrapping up our 2026 Entrepren
 eur in Residence program with a final session on launching your business. 
 We'll map the real funding landscape for a new business in Ontario — sta
 rtup loans\, microloans\, grants\, sponsorship and revenue-based approache
 s — and cover what each one requires\, so you don't waste months applyin
 g to the wrong thing. You'll learn how to present your business to a funde
 r\, and where to find free ongoing support once the series ends. We'll clo
 se with the accountability habits that keep a new business moving.\nThe pr
 ogram includes a short networking component\, providing participants with 
 an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\nRegistration recommen
 ded. Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.\nTo apply for one-on
 -one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Ryan\, please fill out
  the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take f
 orms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bba4341bb11431eea279
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) - Hope + Me
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6ab418b1607483003829095b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Come to a\nvirtual information session\non\
 nOctober 8th at 5-6pm\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\,\nonce a wee
 k for 8 weeks\, October 15 to December 3\n. Registration closes after week
  3\, or when full. Note\, in order to obtain a WRAP certificate at the en
 d of the 8 weeks\, participants need to attend all eight sessions.\nTTC Pr
 esto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for a
 ll participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis
  program is in collaboration with Hope + Me. Hope + Me is solely respons
 ible for the protection of personal information collected through the prog
 ram registration process.\nPlease visit the\nHope and Me website to regist
