BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Internet Horror Classics on Film: We're All Going to the World's F
 air
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T130000
UID:6ab6a294129d8e0031f50829@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this third instalment of Toronto Public Library's virtual s
 eries Internet Horror Classics on Film\, crime writer Kathleen Hale and fi
 lm critic Willow Maclay discuss Jane Schoenbrun's coming-of-age psychologi
 cal horror film\, We're All Going to the World's Fair alongside host Adam 
 Nayman.\nAbout this event's guests:\nKathleen Hale\nis a crime writer base
 d in Los Angeles. Her reporting has been featured in Vanity Fair\, among o
 ther outlets. Slenderman is her first true crime book.\nWillow Maclay\nis 
 a freelance film critic stationed in St. John's\, Newfoundland. She has wr
 itten for outlets such as The Village Voice\, Ebert Voices\, Cinemascope M
 agazine\, and more. She is also the co-author of Corpses\, Fools and Monst
 ers: An Examination of Transgender Cinema.\nAdam Nayman\nis a critic\, tea
 cher\, and author\, whose books include critical surveys of the Coen Broth
 ers\, Paul Thomas Anderson\, and most recently\, in Mind Games\, the filmm
 aker David Fincher. He is a regular contributor to The Ringer\, a lecturer
  at the University of Toronto's Cinema Studies Institute\, and he has writ
 ten on film for The New Yorker and The New York Times.\nRead more:\nCorpse
 s\, Fools and Monsters\nImportant information for accessing this live virt
 ual event:\nYou must register for a free ticket via Eventbrite to gain acc
 ess to this event.\nThis event will be presented in a Zoom Webinar. Once r
 egistered\, you will receive reminder emails from both Zoom and Eventbrite
  with links and instructions to access your unique Zoom Webinar link to wa
 tch this event.\nAt the time of the event\, you must be signed in to Zoom 
 or Eventbrite with the same email address that you used to book your ticke
 t in order to access your unique event link. Unique event links can only b
 e open on one device at a time.\n***\nAccessibility at Toronto Public Libr
 ary\nWe are committed to making our content accessible to as many Toronton
 ians as possible. Please call or email us if you are Deaf or have a disabi
 lity and would like to request accommodation to participate in this progra
 m. Please let us know as far in advance as possible and we will do our bes
 t to meet your request. At least three weeks' notice is preferred. Phone 4
 16-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl.ca\n***\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistrants may be contacted to fill o
 ut a brief survey following the program\n. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerlin
 e@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6a294129d8e0031f50829
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
