BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: My Red Is Not Your Red by Francesco Leka
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261102T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261129T235959
UID:6ac7c2bfa85a2c00337e0e97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of November\, the works of artist Frances
 co Leka are on display at Northern District library.\nFrancesco Leka is a 
 self-taught Canadian artist from Toronto who balances his artistic practic
 e with his studies in Health Sciences at the University of Ottawa. While p
 ursuing a future career in medicine\, he continues to develop his art inde
 pendently and with dedication.\n"In my work\, I find in witnessing viewers
  interpret the densely packed symbolic elements into their own narratives.
  Conceptually\, my works explore the illusions people cling to—nostalgia
 \, order\, wealth—and the harsher truths underlying them. Visually\, sce
 nes in my oil paintings draw inspiration from the awe of nature\, aestheti
 c qualities of myths\, and my own visual interpretations of music."\nThis 
 exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Libra
 ry provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations acr
 oss the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests
  of the city and its neighborhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Nort
 hern District library's opening hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor Art gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac7c2bfa85a2c00337e0e97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
