DESCRIPTION:This program is part of Fort York Library's\nEntrepreneur in R
 esidence\n(EIR) service.\nHow will having “intercultural communication c
 ompetence” help you in your business? As a newcomer\, you have been expo
 sed to different customs\, norms\, values\, and communication styles. Entr
 epreneur in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, teaches you appropri
 ate and effective words\, tones\, body gestures and facial expressions whe
 n you are negotiating with clients\, vendors\, partners\, employees.\nIn t
 his session:\nAdapt your communication in a language that others can under
 stand.\nDisplay more respect\, patience\, and sensitivity to others’ fee
 lings and needs.\nLearn how managing multicultural teams makes you a more 
 effective leader.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nTo apply for one-
