BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T200000
UID:6aaea4c9f9ed2e003851e577@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 1: GETTING STARTED: WORDPRESS FUNDAMENTALS\nThis first sessi
 on introduces participants to the core concepts of the web and the WordPre
 ss\necosystem. We will begin by demystifying domain registration and hosti
 ng services to build a solid\nfoundation for their online presence. Partic
 ipants will learn how to install WordPress and navigate the\ndashboard\, c
 oncluding with a wireframing exercise to plan their website's overall stru
 cture and flow.\nKEYWORDS: DOMAIN REGISTRATION · HOSTING · WORDPRESS INS
 TALLATION · DASHBOARD\nNAVIGATION · WIREFRAMING\nLearners who complete a
 ll the courses will earn a certificate of completion.\n(\nPlease arrive a 
 few minutes early.\nPlease cancel as soon as possible if you are no longer
  available to attend\n.)\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaea4c9f9ed2e003851e577
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
