BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art of Darkness: Edgar Allan Poe's Life & Work
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261204T200000
UID:6a85b6ff4c610f0038954f12@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Professor Emily Ogden shares her intimate inquiry into the sha
 dowy life and compelling work of the definitive author of the macabre.\nSi
 nce Edgar Allan Poe’s mysterious death in 1849\, his stories and poems h
 ave captivated millions of readers around the world. Nearly two centuries 
 later\, why do we continue to descend into the darkness of his imagination
 —and of the genres\, from horror to crime\, that he pioneered?\nIn Darkn
 ess Becomes Bright\, Ogden plumbs the darkness within Poe and enters it al
 ongside him. She interweaves stories from his mysterious and tragic life w
 ith those of his most famous readers and translators\, showing us how Poe
 ’s vision echoes across the generations\, allowing us to make peace with
  our own flawed humanity.\nEmily Ogden speaks with author and critic Naben
  Ruthnum about the brief life and immortal art of Edgar Allan Poe.\nQ&A an
 d book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this event
 ’s guests:\nEmily Ogden\nNaben Ruthnum\nRead more:\nDarkness Becomes Bri
 ght : On the Brief Life and Immortal Art of Edgar Allan Poe\nYour Life Is 
 Mine\nFind You in the Dark\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Blu
 ma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\
 nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registrat
 ion required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the
  greatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guarante
 ed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first s
 erved.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where w
 e host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversat
 ion about their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a br
 ief survey following the program. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b6ff4c610f0038954f12
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
