BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6aaea57d65abe8002a7a853e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 2: BRANDING & HOMEPAGE DESIGN\nThis session focuses on estab
 lishing a professional visual identity for each small business. We will\ne
 xplore how to select and customize themes\, focusing on global design elem
 ents such as typography\nand color palettes that reflect their brand. The 
 session will guide participants through the creation of\nan engaging homep
 age layout designed to capture the audience's attention and communicate th
 eir\ncore value proposition.\nKEYWORDS: VISUAL IDENTITY · THEME CUSTOMIZA
 TION · TYPOGRAPHY & COLOR · HOMEPAGE\nLAYOUT · VALUE PROPOSITION\nLearn
 ers who complete all the courses will earn a certificate of completion.\n(
 \nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nPlease cancel as soon as possible if
  you are no longer available to attend\n.)\nInformation Collection Notice:
 \nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public
  Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(
 d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\,
  delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inf
 ormation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaea57d65abe8002a7a853e
