SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 3
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T200000
UID:6aaea5f8f9ed2e003851e5e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 3: NAVIGATION\, UX & CONTACT INTEGRATION\nThe third session 
 is dedicated to building a seamless and intuitive user journey. We will di
 ve into\ncreating effective navigation menus and professional footers whil
 e utilizing the Elementor page\nbuilder to design functional sub-pages. We
  will also implement professional contact forms and\nintegrate lead genera
 tion tools with participants' email systems\, ensuring visitors can easily
  find\ninformation and connect with the business across all devices.\nKEYW
 ORDS: NAVIGATION MENUS · ELEMENTOR PAGE BUILDER · SUB-PAGES · CONTACT F
 ORMS ·\nLEAD GENERATION\nLearners who complete all the courses will earn 
 a certificate of completion.\n(\nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nPleas
 e cancel as soon as possible if you are no longer available to attend\n.)\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
