BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ghost Stories of Toronto: Modern Phantoms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T130000
UID:6a85b74ce90c830d873fe3bc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As Toronto has grown into a major metropolis\, its ghost stori
 es have grown along with it. Many of our city's most bone-chilling tales w
 ere born out of that rapid evolution — and the sense of unease it has of
 ten caused. We'll conclude this series of talks with author Adam Bunch by 
 exploring ghost stories from Toronto's more recent past. We'll take the su
 bway with the spectre believed to haunt the TTC\, set sail with the ghost 
 ship of Etobicoke Creek\, and meet the demon said to have terrorized one o
 f Canada's most famous folk singers.\nAbout this event's guest:\nAdam Bunc
 h\nRead More:\nThe Toronto Book of Love\nThe Toronto Book of the Dead\nAbo
 ut this series:\nYou can learn a lot about Toronto through its ghost stori
 es. Whether you believe in the supernatural or not\, the tales we tell abo
 ut spirits and spectres illuminate the true history of the city. They're o
 ften tied to dramatic stories of death and disaster\, to fascinating histo
 ric sites\, and to pivotal moments that helped shape our communities. In t
 his series of talks by author Adam Bunch\, we'll explore Toronto's past th
 rough tales of ghosts\, séances and hauntings. Whether it's phantom horse
 s from the War of 1812\, the strange prime minister who believed in the oc
 cult\, or the ghost who was arrested by the Toronto Police Morality Squad\
 , these supernatural stories have a lot to teach us about the history of t
 he place we call home.\n***\nImportant information for accessing this live
  virtual event:\nYou must register for a free ticket via Eventbrite to gai
 n access to this event.\nThis event will be presented in a Zoom Webinar. O
 nce registered\, you will receive reminder emails from both Zoom and Event
 brite with links and instructions to access your unique Zoom Webinar link 
 to watch this event.\nAt the time of the event\, you must be signed in to 
 Zoom or Eventbrite with the same email address that you used to book your 
 ticket in order to access your unique event link. Unique event links can o
 nly be open on one device at a time.\n***\nAccessibility at Toronto Public
  Library\nWe are committed to making our content accessible to as many Tor
 ontonians as possible. Please call or email us if you are Deaf or have a d
 isability and would like to request accommodation to participate in this p
 rogram. Please let us know as far in advance as possible and we will do ou
 r best to meet your request. At least three weeks' notice is preferred. Ph
 one 416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl.ca\n***\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistrants may be contacted to f
 ill out a brief survey following the program\n. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answ
 erline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b74ce90c830d873fe3bc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
