BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Delicious and Surprising History of The Dining Room: Author Ta
 lk with John Ota
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6a8705bbdb86e4004d867404@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:John Ota presents​ and discusses his book\nThe Dining Room\n
 .\nExplore the stories behind twelve iconic dining rooms in homes around t
 he world—from a Japanese samurai house to Claude Monet's brilliant yello
 w dining room to Frida Kahlo's Casa Azul to Jackie Kennedy’s White House
 —and travel through time in pursuit of the ultimate design.​\nThe Dini
 ng Room is an enlightening and joyous celebration of history\, culture and
  the art of dining. Presenter John Ota's charming observations of the surp
 rising impact of dining rooms on our lives and the cherished moments we sh
 are within them will delight armchair travelers\, history fanatics and int
 erior design enthusiasts alike.\nJohn Ota has been involved with architect
 ure and design since 1978\, with degrees from Columbia University\, the Un
 iversity of Toronto and the University of British Columbia. His bestsellin
 g book\nThe Kitchen\nwas a 2021 Taste Canada Awards finalist and a 2021 Pa
 ris Gourmand Cookbook finalist in the book design category. After working 
 in architecture in Toronto\, New York\, and Vancouver\, and as lead on mul
 tiple Ontario Ministry of Culture projects\, John now loves to travel the 
 world visiting historic houses\, cooking regional food\, and meeting peopl
 e of all backgrounds.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8705bbdb86e4004d867404
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
