BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shannon Kyles: What Our Buildings Say About Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261217T200000
UID:6ad7d1f59dbc2b002c8fec9d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Shannon Kyles discusses the history of architecture in Ontario
  and what it says about the people who have built this province. Starting 
 with the Indigenous people\, going through the first century of European c
 ontact\, through the 20th century wars\, democratic policies that resulted
 \, and finally onto the 21st century speculative housing practice.\nProfes
 sor Shannon Kyles is the author of ​\nThe Story of Ontario Architecture\
 n. She has written and published articles on architecture\, taught History
  of Ontario architecture for 42 years at Mohawk College and online for uni
 versities\, and has served on the board of the Architectural Conservancy o
 f Ontario for 15 years.\nRegistration encouraged for event reminders and p
 lanning. Register online at tpl.ca\, by calling 416-393-7674\, or in perso
 n at Bloor/Gladstone branch. Drop-ins also welcome.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7d1f59dbc2b002c8fec9d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
