BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261218T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd106@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Due to renovations the Bookclub will take place in Scadding Co
 urt Community Center in Room 4 (same building)\, participants will be resp
 onsible in sourcing copies of the monthly titles themselves as the branch
  will not be open to the public during this time. We apologize for the inc
 onvenience!\nBecome a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Cl
 ub! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a worl
 d of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming
 -of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something fo
 r everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thin
 gs up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fel
 low readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favo
 rite book? Join us and let's turn the page together!\nFriday November 16: 
 A Gentleman in Moscow by Amor Towles\nSet in Moscow in 1922\,\nA Gentlem
 an in Moscow\nby Amor Towles follows Count Alexander Rostov\, a refined Ru
 ssian aristocrat sentenced by a Bolshevik tribunal to house arrest in the 
 grand Metropol Hotel\, where he must spend the rest of his life confined w
 ithin its walls. As the world outside undergoes dramatic political and soc
 ial change\, the Count gradually transforms his restricted circumstances i
 nto a life rich with unexpected friendships\, meaningful encounters\, and 
 quiet adventures. From navigating the hotel's intricate social world to fo
 rming a particularly meaningful bond with a young girl named Nina\, Rostov
  discovers new perspectives on love\, loyalty\, personal growth\, and the 
 passage of time. Elegant\, witty\, and deeply moving\, the novel explores 
 the nature of freedom\, the importance of human connection\, and the possi
 bility of finding purpose and beauty even when life takes an unexpected tu
 rn.
LOCATION:Sanderson - Closed\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd106
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
