BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sanko Speaks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261219T164500
UID:6aa2f9b53dd190003e7105a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A free\, culturally affirming drop-in program for adults that 
 promotes mental wellness through creative activities\, discussion\, and he
 althy coping strategies. Guided by the concept of Sankofa\, participants e
 xplore connections between past experiences and present wellbeing while bu
 ilding skills for managing stress and supporting mental health. Activities
  vary based on community interests and needs.\nThis program is in collabor
 ation with\nTAIBU Community Health Centre\n.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa2f9b53dd190003e7105a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
