BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Tufting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T200000
UID:6aa0694faafa610029625fd5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:December      2:\nThis workshop will teach participants beginn
 er tufting techniques      and how to start their projects.\nDecember     
  9:\nThis workshop will build on beginner tufting techniques and how to   
    finish their projects.\nDecember      16:\nThis workshop is a self-led 
 tufting session to make space for      participants to create patches for 
 the communal tapestry.\nJanuary      6:\nThis workshop is a self-led tufti
 ng session to make space for      participants to finish their patches for
  the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches to t
 he communal tapestry as they are      completed.\nRegistration required. W
 \norkshop materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Feel f
 ree to drop-in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll also r
 eflect on and discuss our connections to tufting\, the earth\, and our com
 munities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa0694faafa610029625fd5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
