BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Sewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270113T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270113T200000
UID:6aa069533b6c71003e5e9556@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:January      13:\nThis workshop will teach participants functi
 onal sewing techniques      and planning tips to ensure their visions come
  to life.\nJanuary      20:\nThis workshop will teach participants decorat
 ive sewing techniques      and offer space to ideate around their communal
  tapestry patches.\nJanuary      27:\nThis workshop is a self-led sewing s
 ession to make space for      participants to create patches for the commu
 nal tapestry.\nFebruary      3:\nThis workshop is a self-led sewing sessio
 n to make space for      participants to finish their patches for the comm
 unal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches to the commun
 al tapestry as they are      completed.\nRegistration required. Workshop m
 aterials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Feel free to drop
 -in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll also reflect on 
 and discuss our connections to sewing\, fire\, and our communities.\nThis 
 event is part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa069533b6c71003e5e9556
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
